    "summary": "The 3&apos;,5&apos;-cyclic nucleotides cAMP and cGMP function as second messengers in a wide variety of signal transduction pathways. 3&apos;,5&apos;-cyclic nucleotide phosphodiesterases (PDEs) catalyze the hydrolysis of cAMP and cGMP to the corresponding 5&apos;-monophosphates and provide a mechanism to downregulate cAMP and cGMP signaling. This gene encodes a cAMP-specific phosphodiesterase, a member of the cyclic nucleotide phosphodiesterase family.[provided by RefSeq, Apr 2009]",
